+Make a 32 × 32 canvas with transparent and visible pixels in any pixel editor.
+Export RGBA or grayscale-with-alpha PNG at native size, without scaling.
+Colors do not affect the rendered pattern; opacity does.
+
+Open `tools/void-preview.html` directly in a browser and choose the PNG. It
+checks dimensions and transparency and repeats the tile against dark, light
+and adjustable backgrounds. It reads the selected file locally, makes no
+network requests, and neither edits the repository nor publishes anything.
+
+## Apply an approved pattern
+
+Replace `src/assets/void_tile.png` with the approved PNG. Keep its name and
+32 × 32 dimensions. Run `npm run test:unit`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`,
+`npm run build`, `npm run test:web`, `npm run test:ext` and
+`npm run test:obsidian`. The release checks verify the tile header and the
+shared alpha-mask CSS; browser tests verify the built application.
+
+Review the development build before the normal production release from
+`main`. Reverting the asset commit restores the previous pattern. There is no
+design-tool token, synchronization service or staging pipeline to configure.
