+<h1>About cells.garden</h1>
+<p class="lead">A place for projects and tasks to grow into a pixel-art garden.</p>
+<p>Beta 0.2.0 brings the same garden to the web, Chrome and Obsidian. Use it locally without an account, or sign in to sync across devices and collaborate.</p>
+<p>Minerals hold ideas and tasks. Roots hold your reasons. Completed work grows the stem, and results become flowers. A starter plant introduces the layers in a new garden.</p>
+<h2>Free and open source</h2>
+<p>cells.garden is developed by tastefinger, building on Max's original Garden Cells plugin. The source is available under the <a href="https://github.com/lukketsvane/cells.garden/blob/main/LICENSE" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apache-2.0 license</a>.</p>
+<h2>Support the project</h2>
+<p><a href="https://buymeacoffee.com/cells.garden" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Support cells.garden on Buy Me a Coffee</a>. Contributions are optional. There are no paid features to unlock.</p>
+<h2>Report a problem</h2>
+<p><a href="https://github.com/lukketsvane/cells.garden/issues/new" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Create a GitHub issue</a> or email <a href="mailto:cells.garden@proton.me">cells.garden@proton.me</a>. Include the app you are using, its version and steps to reproduce the problem. Do not include passwords, sign-in links or private garden data.</p>
+<h2>Your work stays yours</h2>
+<p>Local gardens stay on the device. Signing in enables optional cloud sync and sharing. Use Export or import in the garden menu to keep a backup. Read the <a href="/privacy.html">privacy policy</a> for details.</p>
+<p><a class="button" href="/">Open the garden</a><a href="/guide/">Read the guide</a></p>
